From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: order NPU TX descriptor publication

The NPU host-adapter worker polls descriptor DONE independently of the
host producer index. It can copy the TXWI and consume the payload address
as soon as that bit becomes visible. The write barrier in the later queue
kick only orders descriptors against the producer-index notification.

Order the TXWI copy and payload address before publishing DONE with a
DMA write barrier and a single control-word store. Keep the existing
queue-kick barrier for the separate index notification. Descriptor bits,
queue bookkeeping and DMA mappings remain the same.

Fixes: 141a81557070 ("wifi: mt76: Introduce the NPU generic layer")
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
--- a/npu.c
+++ b/npu.c
@@ -313,14 +313,20 @@
 {
 	u16 txwi_len = min_t(u16, phy->dev->drv->txwi_size, NPU_TXWI_LEN);
 	struct airoha_npu_tx_dma_desc *desc = (void *)q->desc;
+	u32 ctrl;
 	int ret;
 
+	ctrl = FIELD_PREP(NPU_TX_DMA_DESC_VEND_LEN_MASK, txwi_len) |
+	       FIELD_PREP(NPU_TX_DMA_DESC_LEN_MASK, skb->len) |
+	       NPU_TX_DMA_DESC_DONE_MASK;
+
 	/* TODO: Take into account unlinear skbs */
 	memcpy(desc[q->head].txwi, txwi_ptr, txwi_len);
 	desc[q->head].addr = buf->addr;
-	desc[q->head].ctrl = FIELD_PREP(NPU_TX_DMA_DESC_VEND_LEN_MASK, txwi_len) |
-			     FIELD_PREP(NPU_TX_DMA_DESC_LEN_MASK, skb->len) |
-			     NPU_TX_DMA_DESC_DONE_MASK;
+
+	/* The NPU polls DONE independently of the producer index. */
+	dma_wmb();
+	WRITE_ONCE(desc[q->head].ctrl, ctrl);
 
 	ret = q->head;
 	q->entry[q->head].skip_buf0 = true;
